GUI:Stop
"Stop"
END

GUI:StopDescription
"Stops what the selected units are doing."
END

GUI:ToggleAttackMove
"Attack Move"
END

GUI:ToggleAttackMoveDescription
"Arms attack move: left click where the selected units should go, fighting anything they meet on the way, or drag the left button to spread them along a line. Right click puts it down."
END

GUI:ToggleForceAttack
"Attack"
END

GUI:ToggleForceAttackDescription
"Arms force fire: the next left click is an attack on whatever is under it, your own units and bare ground included. Right click puts it down."
END

GUI:ToggleGuard
"Guard"
END

GUI:ToggleGuardDescription
"Arms guard: left click posts the selected units on that spot, and a left drag posts them along the line you draw. Right click puts it down."
END

GUI:HoldPosition
"Hold Position"
END

GUI:HoldPositionDescription
"Every selected unit guards the spot it is standing on: it shoots what comes into range and never chases it."
END

// Smoke signals.  The three ...Placed lines are what an ally reads; %s is the sender's name.  The
// ...Label words are written over the smoke, which is in the sender's colour.
GUI:SignalAttack
"Signal: Attack"
END

GUI:SignalAttackDescription
"Smoke in your colour and crossed swords on the ground for ten seconds, where the cursor is or on the radar spot under it. Only your allies see it."
END

GUI:SignalDefend
"Signal: Defend"
END

GUI:SignalDefendDescription
"Smoke in your colour and a shield on the ground for ten seconds, where the cursor is or on the radar spot under it. Only your allies see it."
END

GUI:SignalAttention
"Signal: Look Here"
END

GUI:SignalAttentionDescription
"Smoke in your colour and an eye on the ground for ten seconds, where the cursor is or on the radar spot under it. Only your allies see it."
END

GUI:SignalAttackPlaced
"%s: attack here!"
END

GUI:SignalDefendPlaced
"%s: defend here!"
END

GUI:SignalAttentionPlaced
"%s: look here!"
END

GUI:TogglePause
"Pause"
END

GUI:TogglePauseDescription
"Pauses and resumes the game. Single player and replays only."
END

